---
title: "HCML Monitoring Portal: sign-in, session, renewal and sign-out"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant N as nginx
    participant S as Server

    %% The token lives in an HttpOnly cookie, so no script on the page can read it.
    %% Every refusal below is made by the server, whatever the menu shows.

    B->>N: POST /bff/api/auth/login with name, password and the X-HCML-CSRF header
    N->>S: POST /api/auth/login, with a request id added
    S->>S: check the header and the Origin, then the per-account limit and any lock
    S->>S: look the name up and check the scrypt hash, with a decoy check for an unknown name
    S-->>B: 200 and a session cookie (HttpOnly, SameSite Strict), plus the seconds it lasts

    Note over B,S: every later request carries the cookie

    B->>S: GET /api/problems
    S->>S: verify the signature, the issuer and the epoch, then look the user up again
    S->>S: compare the current role with the rule for the route
    S-->>B: 200 with data, or 401 sign in, or 403 wrong role

    B->>S: POST /api/auth/refresh, an hour before the end
    S-->>B: a new cookie

    B->>S: POST /api/auth/logout
    S-->>B: cookie cleared, and the old token is refused from then on
